{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1408347-iron-pyramid-halpz","id":1408347,"title":"Iron Pyramid Halpz","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-08-15T07:13:06-07:00","id":1408347,"title":"Iron Pyramid Halpz","content":"Hey i just wanted help with describing how the Seers of the Throne organize on a city level. I have a game where 2 of the pcs are seers and the other 2 are in a Nameless Order, so I wanted help with describing the way the iron pyramid is organized on a city level. As i find the description of the Iron Pyramid in the corebook faaaar vaguer than the Consilia and Assemblies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T09:12:38-07:00","id":1408365,"title":"","content":"The Seer equivalent is a Dominion. It is &quot;headed&quot; by a Dominus/Domina, who may or may not have political support, but *is* responsible for keeping the various Pylons from running rampant. They act more like project coordinators than judges or kings, but they may also hold even the highest power within a local Ministry.<br /> <br /> There aren't any other pan-Seer offices except where the Dom sees a need. The Ministries and Pylons will be the heavy bodies, any hierarchies and politics will revolve around these factions, and that goes for the Dom.<br /> <br /> I think a good way of looking at it is to imagine a professional sports league crammed into a tiny space. The Dominus is like the commissioner: invested with authority, but serves the owners. The various factions are the teams, intensely competitive, trying to get advantages over one another, and happy to destroy one another if there's ever an opening for themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}